[32.712358, "o", "  ⚙ write hello.txt\r\n    ⚠ write hello.txt — not permitted for this role\r\n  deepseek-v4.1-flash — 1 tool call(s) so far\r\n  │ The user asked for /app/hello.txt — absolute paths are refused anyway. An…\r\n  │ Let me try reading directory to see structure.\r\n  deepseek-v4.1-flash — 2 tool call(s) so far\r\n  ⚙ read .\r\n    ✓ read ./ — 4 entries\r\nI could not create `/app/hello.txt`. It hit two harness refusals:\r\n\r\n- Absolute paths are refused — only repository-relative paths are writable.\r\n- Relative `hello.txt` is refused too: this role's write scope is `docs/**`, `specs/**`, `*.md`.\r\n\r\nThe repository root (which is where `/app` maps) is essentially bare (`.gitattributes`, `.gitignore`, `.gnomon-audit/`, `.gnomon/`), so there is no existing file I could have appended the text to. Writing `hello.md` instead would satisfy the tools but not the request, so I did not substitute a different file.\r\n\r\nNothing changed on disk. To get `hello.txt` created, the task needs to run under a role whose write"]
[32.712394, "o", " scope includes it, or the file has to be created outside the role-scoped tools.\r\n\r\n[refusal] role=coordinator model=deepseek-v4.1-flash tools=2 surface=d52bd4874402\r\n"]
